1	// Q1_0 rdcycle shootout (ace-tq1 style).
2	//
3	//   [2] q1_0_dot_vl256  = ORIGINAL production kernel, called once per row per
4	//                         activation (M*nr calls)
5	//   [3] q1_0_gemv_64x1  = OPTIMIZED row-parallel GEMV, called once per
6	//                         activation (masks re-loaded M times)
7	//   [4] q1_0_gemm_64x1  = GEMM: all M activations in one call, each sign mask
8	//                         loaded once and reused
9	//
10	// Shape: nr=64 rows x n=512 cols x M=4 activations (a 4-token step of the
11	// 2560x1024 matmul). Correctness is proven in llama.cpp/kernel-lab (QEMU,
12	// all VLENs); here a cheap smoke check + cycles. Exit code 0 = pass.
13	//
14	// Build with -DQ1_HVM=1 to put ALL data (x, bricks, y, outputs) in the HVM
15	// vector memory (CSR-discovered, see hvm.h) instead of cached RAM - same
16	// kernels, same checks, only the allocation moves.
17	//
18	// Output is raw _write only - NO stdio. vsim's fpga_l3 engine services the
19	// console MMIO but not the sim_control syscalls stdio init needs (fstat),
20	// so any printf-family call hangs there. QEMU (-mvh) serves _write too.
